course: dictionary
lesson: 3833
title: Forth and back again
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Forth is a small, old-fashioned word. It means forward or onward, away from where you started. «The knight rode forth to fight the dragon.» The knight set off onward, away from the castle, so forth tells you the direction he went.
explain: Forth often hides in phrases. «Back and forth» means one way and then back again, many times. «A pendulum swings back and forth.» The words around forth give you the clue: back tells you the movement goes both ways.
explain: Look for the phrase after the word. «From that day forth» means from then on, and «and so forth» means and other things like these. When you meet forth, read the words before and after it, then swap in your meaning to check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Forth means forward or onward, away from a starting place.
fact: «Back and forth» means going one way and then back again, many times.
fact: «From that time forth» means from then on.
fact: «And so forth» means and other things like these.
fact: Forth is an adverb, a word that tells you how something moves or happens.
exercise: «Mice sweep their whiskers back and forth many times a second.» What does back and forth mean here? | Very fast in a circle | Slowly and quietly | *One way and then back again, many times | Only once, straight ahead
exercise: «A swing is a pendulum: a weight hanging from a point, going back and forth.» What is the pendulum doing? | *Swinging one way and then the other, again and again | Staying perfectly still | Growing bigger each time | Falling to the floor once
exercise: «The knight rode forth.» What does forth mean in this sentence? | Very tired | *Forward or onward, away from where he started | Quietly, in secret | Backwards, home again
test: «From that day forth, Mia always carried a torch.» What does from that day forth mean? | Before that day | Only for one day | *From then on | Never again
test: «Bring sandwiches, drinks, and so forth.» What does and so forth mean? | *and other things like these | and nothing else | and then we leave | and yesterday
exam: «Children with two homes often carry clothes back and forth.» Which meaning fits best? | Throwing clothes away | Buying new clothes | *Going between the two homes many times | Staying in one home all the time
